{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q408418","formula":"C₁₀H₁₆","hill":"C10H16","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":16.0},"names":{"en":"Syntin","ru":"Синтин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Syntin is a hydrocarbon with the molecular formula C10H16 used as a rocket fuel. It is a mixture of four stereoisomers (see below). It has a density of 0.851 g/mL and a boiling point of 158 °C. Due to the presence of three strained cyclopropane rings, the molecule has a highly positive enthalpy of formation: ΔfH°(l) = 133 kJ/mol (980 kJ/kg, the average value for the isomeric mixture), bringing additional energy into the combustion process.","ru":"«Синтин» — разработанное в СССР синтетическое высокоэнергетическое углеводородное ракетное топливо. Применение синтина сходно с применением керосина. Химическая формула — 1-метил-1,2-дициклопропилциклопропан (C10H16)."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":519050,"mass":136.23,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1(CC1C2CC2)C3CC3","inchikey":"GTKAAVZEFUFXDD-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1,2-dicyclopropyl-1-methylcyclopropane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"519050","atoms":26,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.673,"y":0.754,"z":0.103,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.507,"y":0.176,"z":-0.622,"el":"C"},{"x":0.15,"y":1.425,"z":-1.133,"el":"C"},{"x":2.021,"y":0.069,"z":0.1,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.905,"y":0.183,"z":-0.052,"el":"C"},{"x":2.333,"y":-1.073,"z":-0.819,"el":"C"},{"x":2.216,"y":-1.308,"z":0.659,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.395,"y":-0.889,"z":0.876,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.96,"y":-0.78,"z":-0.51,"el":"C"},{"x":0.374,"y":1.443,"z":1.396,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.326,"y":-0.698,"z":-1.244,"el":"H"},{"x":0.73,"y":1.349,"z":-2.046,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.381,"y":2.365,"z":-1.037,"el":"H"},{"x":2.855,"y":0.753,"z":0.263,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.289,"y":1.181,"z":0.167,"el":"H"},{"x":3.325,"y":-1.108,"z":-1.254,"el":"